rustc_codegen_js: never collect a `Vec` in place.

`alloc::vec::in_place_collect` reuses the allocation of a `vec::IntoIter` for the `Vec` an
adapter chain over it collects into, whenever the destination element fits in the source's.
That reinterprets a block of `SRC` elements as a block of `DEST` elements: the buffer pointer is
cast from `*mut SRC` to `*mut DEST` and written through while the rest of the source is still
being read. A heap block on this target is a JavaScript array of one element representation,
retyped at most once, so the cast has an answer only when the two types share a representation;
otherwise it is a compile-time refusal (`(u32, usize)` to `usize`), a run-time one (a newtype to
its field) or a projection into the first element (a one-tuple to its field). Select the
ordinary `from_iter` impls instead, which collect into a fresh allocation.

--- a/library/alloc/src/vec/in_place_collect.rs
+++ b/library/alloc/src/vec/in_place_collect.rs
@@ -166,27 +166,17 @@
